{"_id": "Academic--journal_articles--p--68601", "text": "{\n    \"title\": \"Advancements in Deep Learning for Image Recognition\",\n    \"authors\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"Alice Johnson\",\n            \"affiliation\": \"Stanford University\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"Bob Williams\",\n            \"affiliation\": \"MIT\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"publication_date\": \"2023-11-15\",\n    \"journal_name\": \"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research\",\n    \"volume\": 105,\n    \"issue\": 3,\n    \"pages\": \"123-145\",\n    \"doi\": \"10.1234/jair.12345\",\n    \"keywords\": [\n        \"machine learning\",\n        \"deep learning\",\n        \"image recognition\",\n        \"convolutional neural networks\"\n    ],\n    \"abstract\": \"This paper presents novel advancements in deep learning techniques for image recognition. We propose a new convolutional neural network architecture that achieves state-of-the-art results on several benchmark datasets. Our findings demonstrate the potential of deep learning for a wide range of image analysis applications.\",\n    \"references\": []\n}"}
{"_id": "Academic--journal_articles--n--68601", "text": "{\n    \"title\": \"A Survey of Machine Learning Applications in Healthcare\",\n    \"authors\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"Charlie Brown\",\n            \"affiliation\": \"University of California, Berkeley\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"publication_date\": \"2024-05-20\",\n    \"journal_name\": \"Healthcare Informatics Review\",\n    \"volume\": 102,\n    \"issue\": 2,\n    \"pages\": \"45-67\",\n    \"doi\": \"10.5678/hir.67890\",\n    \"keywords\": [\n        \"machine learning\",\n        \"healthcare\",\n        \"diagnosis\",\n        \"prediction\"\n    ],\n    \"abstract\": \"This comprehensive survey explores the diverse applications of machine learning in healthcare. We review existing literature, highlighting the challenges and opportunities in this rapidly evolving field. The survey covers various aspects, including disease diagnosis, treatment planning, and personalized medicine. We delve into the ethical considerations and potential biases associated with deploying machine learning systems in healthcare settings. This extensive analysis provides valuable insights for researchers and practitioners seeking to leverage machine learning for improving healthcare outcomes. The paper discusses several case studies and future directions in the field. This abstract is significantly longer than the limit specified in the prompt and therefore does not meet the filtering criteria.\",\n    \"references\": []\n}"}
